{"availability":"available","full":"coder-red/scholarcard-overview","name":"scholarcard-overview","description":"Scholarship copilot for Nigerian graduates (live at scholarcard.onrender.com). Public overview: architecture, design decisions, demo. Source is private; access on request.","category":"Design","language":null,"stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-20T19:17:50Z","updated":"2026-09-23T07:59:36Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://scholarcard.onrender.com","topics":["ai-agents","nextjs","nigeria","playwright","scholarships","supabase"],"demo":"https://scholarcard.onrender.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:58.758Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:58.758Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:58.758Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:58.758Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Tell it your degree class, field and NYSC status — it scores every scholarship against your profile, so you apply where you have a real shot, and tracks each one to its deadline.","Live app → · Architecture · How matching works · Stack","Nigerian graduates lose scholarships to two things: not knowing an opportunity exists, and applying to ones they were never eligible for. Generic scholarship sites list everything and rank nothing. ScholarCard does the opposite — it crawls sources continuously, filters for Nigeria-eligible opportunities, and scores each one against your profile (grade fit, field match, visa likelihood, document readiness, past Nigerian winners) so the top of your list is the one you should actually spend a weekend on."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/coder-red/scholarcard-overview/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"caeeaa07645e078b08ec0f0634b45bb255d9a697afa2cf8ccd0a789aab1e4a38","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:58.836Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:58.836Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Tell it your degree class